Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 13:04:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t7000-n102: Enable the display pipe

iBoot leaves the iPod touch 6's 640x1136 MIPI DSI panel running from an
x8r8g8b8 boot framebuffer, the state the ADBE driver adopts after it has
checked that the display DART is in bypass. Enable disp0 so that it
replaces simpledrm, with page flips and vblank interrupts and, once its
self-check of translated scanout passes, scanout of any client buffer
through the display DART.

No panel supply is described, so the panel stays on in system sleep, as
it does under simpledrm. The iPhone 6 and 6 Plus (N61, N56) and the iPad
mini 4 (J96, J97) are left alone: their device trees have not been
compared with this pipe's yet, and the iPad mini 4 drives eDP.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n102.dts | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n102.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n102.dts
index 2893af6..01b9158 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n102.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-n102.dts
@@ -51,6 +51,14 @@
 	power-domains = <&ps_disp0 &ps_mipi_dsi>;
 };
 
+/*
+ * The display pipe takes the 640x1136 panel over from simpledrm. No panel
+ * supply is given: the panel stays on in system sleep.
+ */
+&disp0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &gpu {
 	status = "okay";
 };
